{"astp_version": "0.1.0", "event_type": "turn", "session": {"id": "s-d1dbbee3b48d", "start_time": "2026-09-22T10:40:45.599Z", "user_id": "u-claims-0417", "tenant_id": "thornfield-mutual", "client_app": "claims-copilot", "agent_id": "astp-lab-agent-1", "config_version": "0.2.0"}, "turn": {"index": 0, "timestamp": "2026-09-22T10:40:51.693Z", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5", "model_version": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "tokens_in": 1508, "tokens_out": 103, "latency": 6.0708, "finish_reason": "tool_use"}, "content": {"prompt_text": "What does our reserving guidance say about setting an initial reserve on a new claim?", "prompt_hash": "sha256:35c2f9ad3629a832d68ffc1f7ce464ce9630699fd7862ccbfeb01bf1c01bb4d7", "response_text": "I'll search our reserving guidance documents for information about setting initial reserves on new claims.", "response_hash": "sha256:d2fe72f52f61a91915a6c86f84b4cc7e70de3f132b9d53db4203d81860606986", "system_prompt_version": "sp-0.2.0", "redaction_applied": false}, "control": {"canary_triggered": false, "policy_version": "0.1.0", "block_reason": null}}
{"astp_version": "0.1.0", "event_type": "turn", "session": {"id": "s-d1dbbee3b48d", "start_time": "2026-09-22T10:40:45.599Z", "user_id": "u-claims-0417", "tenant_id": "thornfield-mutual", "client_app": "claims-copilot", "agent_id": "astp-lab-agent-1", "config_version": "0.2.0"}, "turn": {"index": 1, "timestamp": "2026-09-22T10:40:51.952Z", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5", "model_version": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "tokens_in": 9331, "tokens_out": 231, "latency": 0.2577, "finish_reason": "end_turn"}, "content": {"prompt_text": "What does our reserving guidance say about setting an initial reserve on a new claim?", "prompt_hash": "sha256:35c2f9ad3629a832d68ffc1f7ce464ce9630699fd7862ccbfeb01bf1c01bb4d7", "response_text": "According to our reserving guidance (prc-reserving-001), here's what you need to know about setting an initial reserve on a new claim:\n\n**Timing:** Set an opening reserve within one working day of the claim being notified.\n\n**Where information is limited:** Use the class average from the guidance table rather than leaving the reserve at nil. A nil reserve on an open claim is considered a reporting error, not a neutral position.\n\n**Class averages for opening reserves (where information is limited):**\n- Motor, own damage: £2,400\n- Motor, third party property: £3,100\n- Motor, third party injury: £12,000\n- Household, escape of water: £4,800\n- Household, subsidence: £18,000\n- Commercial property: £9,500\n- Professional indemnity: £25,000\n\nThe key principle is that you should always set some reserve when a claim opens, even if you don't have full information yet. Use these benchmarks to ensure you have a reasonable starting point.", "response_hash": "sha256:df8b0981722bfcd792c627f6b46ce8dc659e927ce0c821e1ef69796802ad8576", "system_prompt_version": "sp-0.2.0", "redaction_applied": false}, "control": {"canary_triggered": false, "policy_version": "0.1.0", "block_reason": null}}
